// Title: macOS Apple-Masquerading LaunchAgent or Quarantine Removal
// Description:
// Detects suspicious macOS activity where com.apple.*-named artifacts under user Library
// locations are used with launchctl bootstrap or xattr quarantine removal.
// This behavior was documented in a macOS crypto-draining malware campaign and was
// baseline-validated against 30 days of Defender XDR telemetry with zero matches.
//
// MITRE ATT&CK:
// - T1036.005 Masquerading: Match Legitimate Name or Location
// - T1543.001 Create or Modify System Process: Launch Agent
// - T1553.001 Subvert Trust Controls: Gatekeeper Bypass
//
// Expected Result:
// Low-volume events indicating Apple-masquerading persistence or quarantine removal
// from user-controlled macOS Library locations.
//
// False Positive Notes:
// Legitimate software may use com.apple.* naming, but the combination of:
//   1. com.apple.* artifact naming,
//   2. user Library/Caches or Library/LaunchAgents paths, and
//   3. launchctl bootstrap or xattr quarantine removal
// was not observed in the 30-day enterprise baseline used for validation.
//
// Investigation Guidance:
// - Review the full process ancestry and Terminal/shell activity before the event.
// - Inspect the referenced plist or executable path.
// - Check whether the artifact was recently downloaded or created.
// - Review nearby curl/wget/bash/zsh activity and outbound network connections.
// - Validate code-signing/notarization status and file hash reputation.
// - Hunt for sibling com.apple.* artifacts under the same user Library tree.
//
// Tuning Notes:
// - Avoid broad exclusions for xattr or launchctl; both are common.
// - Tune only after confirming recurring legitimate software in the same path/name pattern.
// - Do not generalize to all com.apple.* artifacts without the user-writable path constraint.
//
// Initiating Article:
// Huntress - macOS crypto-draining malware campaign
// https://www.huntress.com/blog/mac-crypto-draining-malware

let Lookback = 30d;
DeviceProcessEvents
| where Timestamp >= ago(Lookback)
| where
    (
        FileName =~ "xattr"
        and ProcessCommandLine has "com.apple.quarantine"
        and ProcessCommandLine has "/Library/Caches/com.apple."
    )
    or
    (
        FileName =~ "launchctl"
        and ProcessCommandLine has "bootstrap"
        and ProcessCommandLine has "Library/LaunchAgents"
        and ProcessCommandLine has "com.apple."
    )
| extend DetectionReason = case(
    FileName =~ "xattr",
        "Quarantine removal from Apple-masquerading cache path",
    FileName =~ "launchctl",
        "Apple-masquerading LaunchAgent bootstrap",
    "Other"
)
| project
    Timestamp,
    DetectionReason,
    FileName,
    FolderPath,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessParentFileName,
    SHA256
| order by Timestamp desc
